# Pinned synthesis flow. Do not edit without re-recording every baseline.
#
# `-noabc` skips ABC technology mapping. ABC's generic-gate optimisation is
# superlinear on wide arithmetic and took >180s on a 32-multiplier datapath,
# which is unacceptable for a fast eval tier. Everything up to techmap is
# linear-ish and bounded, so wide designs stay cheap to score.
#
# Consequence: cell counts are post-techmap, pre-ABC, so they over-count area.
# They are a deterministic proxy for area, comparable across submissions that
# use this exact flow - not an absolute gate count.
#
# `chparam` pins every parameter the problem fixes before elaboration, so the
# netlist is built for the same parameter values the testbench drives. Without
# it, a submission's defaults could be smaller than the simulated design.
#
# `write_verilog` emits the techmapped netlist. That netlist is what gets
# simulated (with simlib.v), so cells and correctness describe one artifact.
{reads}
{chparams}
hierarchy -check -top {top}
synth -top {top} -flatten -noabc
stat
write_verilog -noattr netlist.v
